{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"t000000000000001","type":"text","x":-1100,"y":-1640,"width":2200,"height":140,"text":"# 🧭 New User Orientation — Claudian Investment Vault\n\nA visual map of architecture, workflows, and the prompt-engineering principles behind the context files."},
		{"id":"g000000000000001","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":-1480,"width":5400,"height":380,"label":"1. What This Vault Is","color":"6"},
		{"id":"n000000000000101","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-1440,"width":5320,"height":300,"text":"## A Second Brain for Non-Consensus Equity Research\n\nA personal knowledge base for institutional-quality equity research, augmented by **Claude Code skills** that mechanically synthesize, cross-link, and propagate insights. Today: **40+ theses, 133+ research notes, 13 sector notes, 6 macro notes**.\n\n**The investment edge** sits in qualitative dimensions the market mis-prices — technology shifts, management quality, competitive dynamics, pricing power, investor bias. Not financial modeling. The objective is **deliberately critical** — not always positive about every opportunity.\n\n**The operating model**: raw material in → skills synthesize structured notes → wikilinks make connections discoverable → propagation keeps everything in sync → **context files prime every LLM session with vault state**. The full reference is [[User Guide]] (76KB); this canvas is the 10-minute orientation.\n\n**Read top-to-bottom**: §1 What → §2 Where (architecture) → §3 How it works (context + prompt-eng) → §4 Process (the loop) → §5 Day-to-day (workflows + notes) → §6 Toolkit (skills) → §7 Guardrails (safety + callouts)."},
		{"id":"g000000000000002","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":-1060,"width":1700,"height":1980,"label":"2. Vault Architecture — 8 Top-Level Directories","color":"2"},
		{"id":"n000000000000201","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-1020,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"## Architecture\n\nFolder = role. Everything has a canonical home; nothing lives at vault root.\n\n**Stats**: 40+ theses · 133+ research · 13 sectors · 6 macro"},
		{"id":"n000000000000202","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-840,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`_Inbox/`** — Drop zone\n\nWeb clips, PDFs, CSVs, raw notes. `/ingest` consumes everything here and moves processed sources to `_Inbox/processed/`."},
		{"id":"n000000000000203","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-660,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Theses/`** — The deliverables\n\nOne file per ticker. Naming: `TICKER - Company Name.md`. **13 structured sections** (Summary → Log). Frontmatter: status, conviction, sector, ticker, source."},
		{"id":"n000000000000204","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-480,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Research/`** — Atomic source notes\n\nNaming: `YYYY-MM-DD - Topic - SourceType.md`. **4 required sections** (Thesis Delta, Summary, Evidence, Contradiction Check). Wikilinked to affected theses."},
		{"id":"n000000000000205","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-300,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Sectors/`** — Map of Content per sector\n\n10 sections. The **Active Theses** list at top doubles as the routing table that sector-scoped skills (`/surface [sector]`, `/prune [sector]`) read."},
		{"id":"n000000000000206","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":-120,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Macro & Technology/`** — Cross-sector\n\nFreeform. Geopolitics, commodities, rates, FX, tech-trend frameworks. Macro shock playbooks live here; sector-specific dynamics belong in Sector notes."},
		{"id":"n000000000000207","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":60,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Templates/`** — Note skeletons (Tier 1 🔒)\n\nDefine vault consistency. Changes here cascade to ALL future skill output. Never edit casually — `/lint` audits template drift across notes."},
		{"id":"n000000000000208","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":240,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`_Archive/`** — Closed positions + snapshots\n\nNever delete — `/_Archive/` preserves history. Houses `Snapshots/` (pre-edit copies from destructive skills) for `/rollback`."},
		{"id":"n000000000000209","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":420,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**`Canvas/`** — Visual relationship maps\n\nThis file lives here. Existing canvases: AI Infrastructure Full Stack, Memory Oligopoly, Pricing Power Matrix, Quality vs Valuation Scatter, Semi Capital Equipment Value Chain."},
		{"id":"n00000000000020a","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":600,"width":1620,"height":280,"text":"## Naming Conventions (enforced)\n\n| Type | Path | Pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| Thesis | `Theses/` | `TICKER - Company Name.md` |\n| Research | `Research/` | `YYYY-MM-DD - Topic - SourceType.md` |\n| Sector | `Sectors/` | `Name.md` (often `@` prefix for tracked-but-no-thesis sectors) |\n| Macro | `Macro & Technology/` | freeform descriptive name |\n\nSource types: `earnings`, `analyst-report`, `news`, `deep-dive`, `data`, `web-clip`, `video-transcript`, `stress-test`, `synthesis`, `brief`, `comparison`, `scenario`, `retro`."},
		{"id":"g000000000000003","type":"group","x":-900,"y":-1060,"width":1700,"height":1980,"label":"3. Context Files — The 'Magic' That Makes the Vault Self-Aware","color":"6"},
		{"id":"n000000000000301","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-1020,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"## The Context Substrate\n\nEvery skill reads these on startup. They're the **prompt-engineering scaffolding** that lets a stateless LLM behave as if it has memory of your vault."},
		{"id":"n000000000000302","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-840,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"📄 [[CLAUDE.md]] — System prompt\n\nDefines vault structure, conventions, writing standards, safety tiers. **Loaded into EVERY session**. This is the behavioral contract. Skills + manual prompts inherit it automatically. Tier 1 protected."},
		{"id":"n000000000000303","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-660,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"📄 [[_hot.md]] — Session cache (~4-5K words)\n\n6 sections: Active Research Thread, Latest Sync, Sync Archive, Recent Conviction Changes, Open Questions, Portfolio Snapshot. **The vault's short-term memory.** Shared writer pool (13 skills update it). Soft/hard caps: 4K / 5K words."},
		{"id":"n000000000000304","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-480,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"📄 [[_graph.md]] — Dependency map\n\nPer-thesis adjacencies + reverse indexes + orphan tracker. Owned exclusively by `/graph` (3 modes: full, `last`, catch-up). Lets `/sync` know which 3-5 thesis files matter for a research note without re-reading all 40."},
		{"id":"n000000000000305","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-300,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"📄 [[_catalyst.md]] — Forward event calendar\n\nRegenerated by `/catalyst` each run. Aggregates catalysts across all positions. Answers 'what's coming up?' without scanning every thesis. Pre-regenerate snapshot protects against mid-run failures."},
		{"id":"n000000000000306","type":"text","x":-860,"y":-120,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"`.last_sync` — Watermark file\n\nmtime = 'last sync ran at'. `/sync` uses `find -newer .last_sync` to detect changed files. **Enables incremental processing** — 30s vs 5min full-vault reads. Deletion triggers full re-read on next sync."},
		{"id":"n000000000000307","type":"text","x":-860,"y":60,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"`_Archive/Snapshots/` — Version control\n\nPre-edit copies from every destructive skill: `TICKER (pre-sync 2026-05-23-2114).md`. `/rollback` restores. Closure snapshots protected 30d. `/clean` purges old. **Encourages aggressive automation — mistakes are cheap to undo.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000308","type":"text","x":-860,"y":240,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"`.graph_invalidations` — Deferred update queue\n\nAppend-only. Closures (`/status active→closed`) queue adjacency deltas here instead of rebuilding the full graph. Consumed and cleared by next `/graph last`. `/lint` flags stale invalidations."},
		{"id":"n000000000000309","type":"text","x":-860,"y":420,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"`.rename_incomplete.TICKER` — Failure marker\n\nDropped by `/rename` if any wikilink rewrite fails. **Hard-blocks every ticker-scoped skill on TICKER** until resolved. Prevents stale state from cascading. Re-run `/rename` with same args to retry failed Edits."},
		{"id":"n00000000000030a","type":"text","x":-860,"y":600,"width":1620,"height":280,"text":"## Other Coordination Files\n\n| File | Owner | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.sync_all_fresh` | `/sync all` | Forces next `/graph` into full rebuild |\n| `.locks/` | All write skills | Vault locks — vault-wide vs ticker:TICKER vs read-only |\n| `.archive_ticker_registry.md` | `/status closure`, `/prune` | Append-only ledger; `/thesis` reads for archive-collision detection |\n| `_sync-manifest`, `_status-manifest`, etc. | Per-skill | Mid-run state; restartable on crash; consumed on success |\n\nAll of these are git-tracked. Every read by every skill is reproducible."},
		{"id":"g000000000000004","type":"group","x":1000,"y":-1060,"width":1700,"height":1980,"label":"4. Prompt-Engineering Principles","color":"6"},
		{"id":"n000000000000401","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-1020,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"## How Context Engineering Works\n\nThe context files in §3 aren't conveniences — they implement specific prompt-engineering patterns that let a stateless LLM behave as a coherent agent over months of vault evolution."},
		{"id":"n000000000000402","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-840,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**1. System prompt as durable memory**\n\n[[CLAUDE.md]] ≈ injected system prompt every session. Stable behavioral contract — no fine-tuning needed. Define a convention once → all skills + manual prompts inherit it. Updating CLAUDE.md updates the LLM's worldview for all future calls."},
		{"id":"n000000000000403","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-660,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**2. Context cache pattern (`_hot.md`)**\n\nLLMs are stateless across sessions. `_hot.md` is custom short-term memory. Skills write deltas; users read on session start. 6 sections, soft cap 4K words — enough for resume, small enough to fit in any prompt budget."},
		{"id":"n000000000000404","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-480,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**3. Dependency graph priming**\n\n`_graph.md` tells skills which 3-5 thesis files matter for a given research note. Without it, `/sync` would read all 40 theses every time. With it: incremental, scoped, fast. **Avoids cold-context re-reads.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000405","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-300,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**4. Snapshot-based rollback**\n\nEvery destructive skill copies the file before editing. `_Archive/Snapshots/...`. `/rollback` restores any snapshot. Effect: **destructive operations become reversible** → enables aggressive automation."},
		{"id":"n000000000000406","type":"text","x":1040,"y":-120,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**5. Subagent forking for context isolation**\n\n`/lint`, `/prune`, `/surface`, `/retro` fork to a subagent. They read hundreds of files; only the final report returns to main. Your main-conversation context stays clean — heavy reads don't poison the session."},
		{"id":"n000000000000407","type":"text","x":1040,"y":60,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**6. Watermark-based incrementality**\n\n`.last_sync` mtime = the watermark. `find -newer` returns only files modified since. Drives `/sync` graph-assisted mode. Same pattern: `/graph last` uses thesis mtimes + `.graph_invalidations` to skip unchanged files."},
		{"id":"n000000000000408","type":"text","x":1040,"y":240,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**7. Pre-flight contract (locks + markers + probes)**\n\nEvery write-skill runs 4 checks at Step 0: vault lock acquisition, rename-marker check, name sanitization, section existence probe. **Prevents concurrent races + cascading failures.** Spec at `.claude/skills/_shared/preflight.md`."},
		{"id":"n000000000000409","type":"text","x":1040,"y":420,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**8. Append-only audit logs**\n\nThesis `## Log` sections are append-only with prefix classification. `/sync` reads the prefix to decide propagation (skill-origin vs research-driven). The audit trail IS the source-of-truth for 'what changed when' and 'should this trigger downstream updates'."},
		{"id":"n00000000000040a","type":"text","x":1040,"y":600,"width":1620,"height":160,"text":"**9. Provenance immutability**\n\n`source:` frontmatter never changes. Research note bodies are immutable. Provenance + audit trail = post-hoc evidence reconstruction in 90 days when defending a thesis. **The vault is its own court of record.**"},
		{"id":"n00000000000040b","type":"text","x":1040,"y":780,"width":1620,"height":140,"text":"**10. Deterministic skill specifications**\n\nSkills live in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` as self-contained specs (pre-flight, steps, exit conditions). **Reproducible behavior regardless of model temperature.** Long skills include a truncation safeguard — re-Read full spec before mutating."},
		{"id":"g000000000000006","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":960,"width":5400,"height":900,"label":"5. The Core Loop — Two Complementary Cycles","color":"5"},
		{"id":"n000000000000601","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":1000,"width":5320,"height":140,"text":"## The Core Loop\n\nTwo loops drive every session. **Forward loop** moves new information into the vault. **Backward loop** reviews thinking against market reaction. Periodic maintenance keeps the substrate healthy. Read-only chains (`/brief`, `/lint`, `/rollback list`) skip `/graph last`."},
		{"id":"n000000000000602","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":1160,"width":1740,"height":660,"text":"### Forward Loop — New info in\n\n```\n_Inbox drop\n   ↓\n/ingest           ← raw → structured Research notes\n   ↓\n/sync             ← propagate to affected Theses/Sectors/Macro/_hot.md\n   ↓\n[research, analysis, callouts]\n   ↓\n/sync             ← propagate your additions\n   ↓\n/graph last       ← reconcile dependency map\n```\n\n**`/ingest`** — pulls URL or batch-processes `_Inbox/`. Creates Research notes only.\n\n**`/sync`** — 3 modes:\n- default (graph-assisted): reads changed files + adjacencies\n- `/sync TICKER`: scoped to one thesis\n- `/sync all`: brute-force re-reads everything\n\n**`/graph last`** — incremental: changed theses + `.graph_invalidations`. ~5 seconds.\n\n**Always pair `/ingest` with `/sync`.** Ingest only creates research notes — sync propagates them into theses + sectors + macro."},
		{"id":"n000000000000603","type":"text","x":-880,"y":1160,"width":1740,"height":660,"text":"### Backward Loop — Thinking vs market\n\n```\n/retro [1w|1m|1q]   ← aggregate callouts + Logs vs price + news + earnings\n   ↓\n[review]            ← see what market priced vs what you thought\n   ↓\n/status · /deepen · /stress-test    ← act on findings\n   ↓\n/sync               ← propagate the acts\n   ↓\n/graph last         ← reconcile\n```\n\n**`/retro`** ranks trade ideas by **narrative-price gap**:\n\n| Delta | Meaning | Weight |\n|---|---|---|\n| aligned | Already priced | 0 |\n| **inverted-bear** | Good news, price fell | 1.5× |\n| **inverted-bull** | Bad news, price rose | 1.5× |\n| unreactive | Event happened, price flat | 2.0 |\n\nVault stance × news polarity × price → **alpha harvest**, **missed signal**, or **stress-test candidate**.\n\nNever auto-mutates conviction — Tier 3 confirmation required."},
		{"id":"n000000000000604","type":"text","x":900,"y":1160,"width":1740,"height":660,"text":"### Periodic Maintenance\n\n**`/surface`** — Forward: new ideas, blind spots, contrarian signals. Default mode is fast (section-targeted); `/surface all` is comprehensive but ~4× cost. **Forks to subagent** — main context stays clean.\n\n**`/catalyst`** — Forward: refresh event calendar across all positions. Web-searches earnings dates. Flags clusters and gaps.\n\n**`/lint`** — Now: vault health (structural, freshness, analytical). Use `/lint TICKER` for scoped checks.\n\n**`/archive-callouts`** — Now: sweep ≥180d addressed callouts into per-thesis `## Legacy Callouts` archive.\n\n**`/prune`** — Now: evaluate weak/stale/low-conviction theses for upgrade/monitoring/closure. Always run `/sync` first (warns if unsynced research exists).\n\n**Cadence**:\n- Weekly: `/retro 1w`, `/surface`, `/catalyst`\n- Monthly: `/retro 1m`, full maintenance chain\n- Quarterly: `/retro 1q`, `/surface all`, `/prune`, `/archive-callouts`"},
		{"id":"g000000000000007","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":1900,"width":2650,"height":1700,"label":"6a. Major Workflows — Skill Chains","color":"5"},
		{"id":"n000000000000701","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":1940,"width":2570,"height":140,"text":"## Workflow Chains\n\nMulti-skill sequences for common scenarios. Each chain is the minimum sequence. See [[User Guide#3. Workflow Chains]] for variants and edge cases."},
		{"id":"n000000000000702","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":2100,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### New position — full build\n\n```\n/thesis TICKER\n/status TICKER status draft→active [rationale]\n/stress-test TICKER\n/sync TICKER\n```\n\nOptional: `/compare TICKER vs COMPETITOR` before `/sync`, `/deepen TICKER [weakest section]` to fill gaps."},
		{"id":"n000000000000703","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":2280,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### Earnings reaction\n\n```\n/ingest [transcript or press release URL]\n/sync TICKER\n/status TICKER conviction old→new [if needed]\n```\n\nIf ambiguous: `/stress-test TICKER` before deciding on conviction change."},
		{"id":"n000000000000704","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":2460,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### Conviction drift response\n\n```\n/sync flags ⚠️\n   ↓\n/stress-test TICKER         ← investigate\n/status TICKER conviction old→new [rationale]   ← or 'reaffirm'\n/sync TICKER\n```\n\nOr `/deepen TICKER [section]` for targeted research before status change."},
		{"id":"n000000000000705","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":2640,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### Macro shock (Fed cut, geopolitics, oil)\n\n```\n/scenario [event with quantitative params]\n/status TICKER conviction old→new [transmission channel]\n/compare [exposed] vs [beneficiary]\n/sync\n```\n\nScenario auto-flags Major-impact theses in their Logs."},
		{"id":"n000000000000706","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":2820,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### Adversarial pressure test\n\n```\n/stress-test TICKER\n/deepen TICKER [section the stress test flagged]\n/sync TICKER\n```\n\nAlways run before major sizing decisions or before pitching to others."},
		{"id":"n000000000000707","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":3000,"width":2570,"height":280,"text":"### Monthly maintenance chain\n\n```\n/sync all          ← brute-force consistency baseline\n/graph             ← full graph rebuild\n/lint              ← health check\n/prune             ← evaluate weak theses\n/clean             ← purge old snapshots\n/surface           ← find new ideas (forked subagent)\n/catalyst          ← refresh event calendar\n/graph last        ← pick up closure invalidations\n```\n\nRun in this order. Forked subagents (`/lint`, `/prune`, `/surface`) keep main context clean. Full chain on a 41-thesis vault: ~460K context (well under 1M cap)."},
		{"id":"n000000000000708","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":3300,"width":2570,"height":160,"text":"### Recovery — undo bad sync\n\n```\n/rollback TICKER       ← pick (pre-sync) snapshot\n/sync TICKER           ← OR /sync all if cascade\n/graph                 ← full rebuild after closure\n```\n\nCascade detection: multi-file sync offers atomic multi-file restore. Diff shown before confirming."},
		{"id":"g000000000000005","type":"group","x":50,"y":1900,"width":2650,"height":1700,"label":"6b. Note Anatomy — The 4 Note Types","color":"3"},
		{"id":"n000000000000501","type":"text","x":90,"y":1940,"width":2570,"height":140,"text":"## Note Types\n\nEvery note has a canonical structure. Skills (and `/lint`) enforce it. Frontmatter is mandatory across all types."},
		{"id":"n000000000000502","type":"text","x":90,"y":2100,"width":2570,"height":380,"text":"### Thesis Note — `Theses/TICKER - Name.md` (14 sections)\n\nTemplate: [[Templates/Thesis Template]]\n\n1. **Summary** — one-paragraph investment case\n2. **Key Non-consensus Insights** — 3-5 paragraphs of what market is missing\n3. **Outstanding Questions** — 3-10 IC-style questions\n4. **Business Model & Product Description** — deep breakdown\n5. **Industry Context** — competitive dynamics, value chain\n6. **Key Metrics** — table (Market Cap, EV/Rev, Growth, GM, FCF Yield)\n7. **Bull Case** — explicit upside scenario\n8. **Bear Case** — explicit downside scenario\n9. **Catalysts** — near-term price-moving events\n10. **Risks** — what breaks the thesis\n11. **Conviction Triggers** — falsifiable `→ HIGH if` / `→ LOW if` / `→ CLOSE if`\n12. **Related Research** — wikilinks to supporting notes\n13. **Legacy Callouts** — auto-managed archive (owned by `/archive-callouts`)\n14. **Log** — append-only dated entries (max 2 lines each)\n\nFrontmatter: `date, tags, status, conviction, sector, ticker, source`"},
		{"id":"n000000000000503","type":"text","x":90,"y":2500,"width":2570,"height":320,"text":"### Research Note — `Research/YYYY-MM-DD - Topic - Type.md` (4 sections)\n\nTemplate: [[Templates/Research Template]]\n\n1. **Thesis Delta** — 1-2 sentences: what this changes for the investment case\n2. **Summary** — 1-4 paragraphs capturing source's argument, mechanism, scope\n3. **Evidence** — data points only. Tables preferred. No narrative.\n4. **Contradiction Check** — does this support or challenge existing conviction? Be specific.\n5. *(optional)* **Source Excerpts**, **Framework**, **Key Segments** (>15K words)\n\n**Body length scales with source word count**: <1.5K → ≥300; 1.5-5K → ≥800; 5-15K → ≥1.8K; >15K → ≥2.5K + Key Segments.\n\nFrontmatter: `date, tags, status, sector, ticker, source, source_type`"},
		{"id":"n000000000000504","type":"text","x":90,"y":2840,"width":2570,"height":320,"text":"### Sector Note — `Sectors/Name.md` (10 sections)\n\nTemplate: [[Templates/Sector Template]]\n\nActs as a **Map of Content** for the sector. Sector-scoped skills route via the Active Theses list.\n\n1. **Active Theses** — wikilinks to all active theses (MOC nav, draft theses excluded)\n2. **Key industry questions**\n3. **Industry history**\n4. **Competitive dynamics**\n5. **Product-level analysis**\n6. **Acquisitions and new entrants**\n7. **Macro shifts**\n8. **Investor heuristics** — what's priced in vs where consensus could be wrong\n9. **Related Research**\n10. **Legacy Callouts** + **Log**\n\n**Important**: draft theses are intentionally invisible to sector-scoped skills. Promote to active before running `/surface [sector]`."},
		{"id":"n000000000000505","type":"text","x":90,"y":3180,"width":2570,"height":200,"text":"### Macro Note — `Macro & Technology/Name.md` (freeform)\n\nGeo / rates / commodities / tech trends. **Freeform by design** — covers macro shock playbooks, trading opportunities, portfolio re-allocation strategies. Cross-sector reach.\n\nSector-specific industry dynamics belong in Sector notes, not here. Macro is for variables that move multiple sectors at once.\n\nExamples in vault: `Iran War Trading Playbook`, `800VDC Adoption`, `AI Bubble Risk and Semiconductor Valuations`, `Stablecoin Regulation as Geopolitical Infrastructure`."},
		{"id":"g000000000000008","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":3680,"width":5400,"height":1480,"label":"7. Skills Inventory","color":"4"},
		{"id":"n000000000000801","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":3720,"width":5320,"height":80,"text":"## Skills Inventory — 19 Skills in 4 Categories\n\nEvery skill has a canonical entry in [[User Guide#5. Skill Reference|§5 Skill Reference]] (args, what it creates, what it modifies, follow-up)."},
		{"id":"n000000000000802","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":3820,"width":1280,"height":80,"text":"### Core (4)\n\nThe daily-driver loop"},
		{"id":"n000000000000812","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":3820,"width":1280,"height":80,"text":"### Analytical (6)\n\nGenerate insight"},
		{"id":"n000000000000822","type":"text","x":-20,"y":3820,"width":1280,"height":80,"text":"### Building (3)\n\nCreate / improve content"},
		{"id":"n000000000000832","type":"text","x":1300,"y":3820,"width":1280,"height":80,"text":"### Maintenance (6)\n\nKeep vault healthy"},
		{"id":"n000000000000803","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":3920,"width":1280,"height":280,"text":"**`/ingest`**\nURL, file path, or batch `_Inbox/`. Creates Research notes. Moves source to processed. Same-source dedup. **Always follow with `/sync`.**\n\n**`/sync`**\nPropagates new research into Theses + Sectors + Macro + `_hot.md`. Modes: default (graph-assisted), `TICKER` (scoped), `all` (brute-force)."},
		{"id":"n000000000000804","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":4220,"width":1280,"height":280,"text":"**`/status`**\nConviction change or status transition. `/status NVDA conviction high→medium [reason]`. Tier 3 confirmation required (except `draft→active` fast-path). Creates snapshot.\n\n**`/graph`**\nThree modes: `/graph` (full rebuild), `/graph last` (incremental), `/graph 3` (catch-up N days). Owned exclusively by this skill."},
		{"id":"n000000000000813","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":3920,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/surface`**\nNew ideas, blind spots. 4 modes: default (fast), `all` (deep, 4× cost), `TICKER`, `[sector]`. **Forks to subagent.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000814","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":4120,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/stress-test`**\nActs as short seller. Flags for conviction reassessment but never auto-changes conviction. Output is a Research note."},
		{"id":"n000000000000815","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":4320,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/scenario`**\n'What if Fed cuts 150bps', 'China invades Taiwan'. Propagates through portfolio. Auto-flags Major-impact theses."},
		{"id":"n000000000000816","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":4520,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/compare`**\nSide-by-side competitive analysis. 2+ tickers. At least one must have a thesis; missing tickers use web research."},
		{"id":"n000000000000817","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":4720,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/catalyst`**\nRegenerates `_catalyst.md`. Web-searched earnings dates. Flags catalyst clusters and gaps."},
		{"id":"n000000000000818","type":"text","x":-1340,"y":4920,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/retro`**\n1w/1m/1q backward review. Narrative-price gap ranking. **Forks to subagent.** Auto-appends `Retro insight:` Log entry to Top-3 trade ideas."},
		{"id":"n000000000000823","type":"text","x":-20,"y":3920,"width":1280,"height":380,"text":"**`/thesis`**\nCreates new thesis (draft, 14 sections). Searches vault first (research, sector, macro), then web. Archive-collision detection if archived thesis exists for TICKER."},
		{"id":"n000000000000824","type":"text","x":-20,"y":4320,"width":1280,"height":380,"text":"**`/deepen`**\nSurgical section enhancement (NOT full rewrite). 11 named sections + auto-detect mode. Pre-edit snapshot. Optional supporting Research note."},
		{"id":"n000000000000825","type":"text","x":-20,"y":4720,"width":1280,"height":380,"text":"**`/brief`**\n1-page IC-style memo from thesis. Read-only on thesis. Excludes all callouts and Legacy archive. Pure derivative; updates `_hot.md` only."},
		{"id":"n000000000000833","type":"text","x":1300,"y":3920,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/lint`**\nVault health: structural, freshness, analytical. Full or `TICKER`-scoped. **Forks to subagent.** Read-only report."},
		{"id":"n000000000000834","type":"text","x":1300,"y":4120,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/prune`**\nEvaluate weak/stale/low theses. Approval gate before applying. Warns if unsynced research exists. **Forks to subagent.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000835","type":"text","x":1300,"y":4320,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/clean`**\nPurge old snapshots from `_Archive/Snapshots/`. Default 180d. Orphan + closure-snapshot + modified-source safety nets."},
		{"id":"n000000000000836","type":"text","x":1300,"y":4520,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/archive-callouts`**\nSweep ≥180d addressed callouts into `## Legacy Callouts`. Default dry-run; explicit threshold = execute. `[[pinned]]` opt-out."},
		{"id":"n000000000000837","type":"text","x":1300,"y":4720,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/rollback`**\nRestore from snapshot. Lists or restores. Cascade detection for multi-file syncs. Pre-rollback safety snapshot."},
		{"id":"n000000000000838","type":"text","x":1300,"y":4920,"width":1280,"height":180,"text":"**`/rename`**\nCompany name changes (FB→META). Atomic mv + rewrites all wikilinks + graph header + sector entry + snapshots. **Always run `/graph` (full) after.**"},
		{"id":"g000000000000009","type":"group","x":-2700,"y":5240,"width":2650,"height":1380,"label":"8. Safety & Change Discipline","color":"1"},
		{"id":"n000000000000901","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":5280,"width":2570,"height":140,"text":"## 3-Tier Change Safety\n\nNot all edits are equal. Tiered model: protected → append-only → confirmation-required. Operational rules backstop the tiers."},
		{"id":"n000000000000902","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":5440,"width":2570,"height":260,"text":"### Tier 1: Protected 🔒\nNever modify without explicit instruction.\n\n- **CLAUDE.md** — system instructions; structural changes need explicit ask\n- **Templates/*.md** — define vault consistency; changing them alters all future output\n- **.obsidian/** — Obsidian config\n- **.claude/skills/** — skill definitions\n\nViolation: changes the LLM's behavior or breaks every future skill run."},
		{"id":"n000000000000903","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":5720,"width":2570,"height":260,"text":"### Tier 2: Append-Only Zones ➕\nAdd at the end; never edit/reorder/delete existing entries.\n\n- **Thesis `## Log` sections** — dated entries appended to end\n- **`_hot.md ## Sync Archive`** — prepend new, never remove old\n- **Research notes** (once created) — body content immutable; corrections go in new note or thesis log\n\nViolation: breaks the audit trail / provenance chain."},
		{"id":"n000000000000904","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":6000,"width":2570,"height":300,"text":"### Tier 3: Confirmation Required ❓\nThese are investment decisions, not formatting. Confirm with user before applying.\n\n- `conviction:` frontmatter changes (high→medium etc.)\n- `status:` transitions (active→monitoring, active→closed)\n- Moving a thesis to `/_Archive`\n- Removing any wikilink from thesis/sector/macro\n- Deleting or renaming any file (use archive-not-delete)\n\nExceptions: `draft→active` and `reaffirm` skip the prompt (additive, no analytical content change)."},
		{"id":"n000000000000905","type":"text","x":-2660,"y":6320,"width":2570,"height":260,"text":"### Operational Rules (skim list)\n\n1. **Read before write** — never `Write` an existing file without `Read` first\n2. **Archive, don't delete** — preserves log history + link traceability\n3. **`source:` frontmatter is immutable** — provenance record\n4. **New files to correct dir** — never create vault content at root\n5. **Follow naming conventions** (see Architecture group)\n6. **Check before creating** — search vault for existing notes on ticker/topic\n7. **Wikilinks are additive** — adding is free; removing requires explicit instruction\n8. **Batch operation transparency** — multi-file skills report every change\n9. **`_hot.md` auto-create + compression contract** — schema enforced by `/lint`\n10. **Pre-flight contract** — 4 checks at Step 0 for every write skill\n11. **Truncation safeguard** — re-Read full SKILL.md if `<system-reminder>` truncated"},
		{"id":"g00000000000000a","type":"group","x":50,"y":5240,"width":2650,"height":1380,"label":"9. Inline Callouts — Feedback Markers","color":"4"},
		{"id":"n000000000000a01","type":"text","x":90,"y":5280,"width":2570,"height":140,"text":"## Inline Callouts\n\nVisual hotkey-driven markers for feedback on LLM-generated content. Drop them inline; ask Claude to address; the response stays as audit trail. **The lightweight feedback channel.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000a02","type":"text","x":90,"y":5440,"width":2570,"height":260,"text":"### The 4 Types\n\n| Callout | Hotkey | Color | Use when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `> [!question]` | Mod+Alt+1 | Yellow ❓ | Ask a question |\n| `> [!error]` | Mod+Alt+2 | Red ⚡ | Flag disagreement |\n| `> [!tip]` | Mod+Alt+3 | Teal 🔥 | Suggest a change |\n| `> [!todo]` | Mod+Alt+4 | Blue ☑ | Specify an action |\n\n`Mod` = ⌘ on macOS, Ctrl on Windows/Linux. Templates at `Templates/_callouts/user-*.md`. Setup via Templater hotkeys (one-time per vault clone)."},
		{"id":"n000000000000a03","type":"text","x":90,"y":5720,"width":2570,"height":280,"text":"### Lifecycle\n\n| State | Header pattern | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Fresh** | `> [!type] YYYY-MM-DD` alone | Unresolved |\n| **Addressed** | `... → Addressed YYYY-MM-DD` + `Prompt:` + `Response:` blocks | Claude responded |\n| **Pinned** | header contains `[[pinned]]` | Persistent revisit slot — exempt from sweep |\n| **Legacy** | plain bullet in `## Legacy Callouts` | Swept by `/archive-callouts` after 180d |\n\n`[[pinned]]` is an intentionally unresolved wikilink — `/graph` and `/lint` skip it. **Don't create `pinned.md`.**"},
		{"id":"n000000000000a04","type":"text","x":90,"y":6020,"width":2570,"height":280,"text":"### Workflow\n\n```\n1. Drop callout inline (Mod+Alt+1..4)\n2. Continue writing — callout is a flag, not a blocker\n3. Ask Claude: 'Address fresh callouts in [[note]]'\n4. Claude edits sections in-place, marks as Addressed,\n   writes Log entry prefixed 'Addressed user callouts:'\n5. /sync TICKER → /graph last\n```\n\n**Critical**: prefix the Log entry with `Addressed user callouts:` (or `Manual edit:`). Skill-origin prefixes (`Deepened:`, `Status change:`) silently skip sector/macro propagation."},
		{"id":"n000000000000a05","type":"text","x":90,"y":6320,"width":2570,"height":260,"text":"### Callout-is-Ledger / Body-is-Deliverable Rule\n\nFull analysis lives in **body section**; callout `Response:` is a **1-3 sentence ledger entry + pointer**.\n\n**Why**: callouts get swept to `## Legacy Callouts` after 180d. Content living only in callouts is invisible to `/brief`, `/deepen`, `/sync`, and any reader scanning the note's spine. The callout = audit trail of the exchange; the body = evergreen knowledge.\n\n**Anti-pattern**: multi-paragraph Response with tables. Tighten the Response; move substance to body."},
		{"id":"t000000000000999","type":"text","x":-2700,"y":6680,"width":5400,"height":160,"text":"## 📚 Further Reading\n\n- [[User Guide]] — Full reference manual (76 KB): all chains, all skills, all gotchas. Scan §4 'I Want To...' to find the right workflow from intent.\n- [[CLAUDE.md]] — System prompt + safety tiers + operational rules. The behavioral contract every skill inherits.\n- [[INFRASTRUCTURE.md]] — Deep mechanics: how skills coordinate via locks, manifests, snapshots. Read when lint flags something weird or you want to understand the internals.\n- [[_hot.md]] — Your current session state. Read on session start to resume context.\n- [[_graph.md]] — The vault dependency map. Updated by `/graph`.\n- Existing canvases: [[Canvas/AI Infrastructure Full Stack.canvas|AI Infrastructure Full Stack]] · [[Canvas/Memory Oligopoly.canvas|Memory Oligopoly]] · [[Canvas/Pricing Power Matrix.canvas|Pricing Power Matrix]]"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"e000000000000001","fromNode":"g000000000000003","fromSide":"right","toNode":"g000000000000004","toSide":"left","label":"implement these patterns","color":"6"},
		{"id":"e000000000000002","fromNode":"g000000000000002","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"g000000000000005","toSide":"top","label":"directories house these note types","color":"2"},
		{"id":"e000000000000003","fromNode":"g000000000000006","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"g000000000000007","toSide":"top","label":"composed into these chains","color":"5"},
		{"id":"e000000000000004","fromNode":"g000000000000007","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"g000000000000008","toSide":"top","label":"chains call these skills","color":"4"}
	]
}